<article class="env-lemma" id="04YP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04YP">Lemma <span data-tag="04YP">101.3.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. Let $T$ be a scheme and let $x, y$ be objects of the fibre category of $\mathcal{X}$ over $T$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathit{Isom}_\mathcal {X}(y, y)$ is a group algebraic space over $T$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathit{Isom}_\mathcal {X}(x, y)$ is a pseudo torsor for $\mathit{Isom}_\mathcal {X}(y, y)$ over $T$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See Groupoids in Spaces, Definitions <a href="/tag/043H" data-tag="043H">78.5.1</a> and <a href="/tag/04TW" data-tag="04TW">78.9.1</a>. The lemma follows immediately from the fact that $\mathcal{X}$ is a stack in groupoids. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>